<PolicyLayout
    title="Consent, Assumption of Risk, Release & Emergency Authorization"
    description="STEM+C participant consent, assumption of risk, release of liability, emergency authorization, and optional media authorization for program participants and their families."
    effective="August 14, 2026"
    noticeTitle="Approved for signature"
    noticeTone="info"
    notice="This document has been approved by legal counsel and may be circulated for signature. It is not to be relied upon as a substitute for appropriate insurance, training, supervision, machine guarding, written safety procedures, or compliance with applicable law."
  pdf="/policies/stemplusc-consent-release.pdf"
>
  <p>
    This Consent, Assumption of Risk, Release, Hold Harmless, and Emergency Authorization
    (this &ldquo;Agreement&rdquo;) relates to participation by the person identified during
    registration (the <strong>&ldquo;Participant&rdquo;</strong>) in activities of
    <strong>STEM+C</strong>. If the Participant is under 18 years of age, this Agreement must
    also be signed by the Participant&rsquo;s parent or legal guardian (the
    <strong>&ldquo;Parent/Guardian&rdquo;</strong>). The Participant and Parent/Guardian are referred
    to together as the <strong>&ldquo;Signing Parties.&rdquo;</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Important notice</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Please read this entire Agreement carefully. It describes serious hazards, including hazards
      from industrial machinery, fabrication equipment, robots, electricity, batteries, chemicals,
      and travel. It also contains a release of claims, including certain claims based on ordinary
      negligence, and may affect legal rights.
    </strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Signing this Agreement does not replace STEM+C&rsquo;s responsibility to maintain and enforce
    appropriate safety rules, training, supervision, equipment safeguards, and insurance.
  </p>

  <h2>Definitions</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>&ldquo;Activities&rdquo;</strong> means all STEM+C-sponsored, organized, or approved
    activities, whether occurring at a STEM+C location or elsewhere. Activities include team
    meetings; shop and build sessions; design, construction, programming, inspection, testing,
    maintenance, repair, and operation of robots and other devices; training; outreach,
    demonstrations, fundraising, league play, and competitions; loading and unloading; and travel,
    lodging, meals, and other activities incidental to those events.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>&ldquo;STEM+C&rdquo;</strong> means <strong>STEM+C</strong>, an Arizona nonprofit
    corporation, Arizona Corporation Commission Entity ID 1949945, EIN 83-3523903.
    <strong>&ldquo;Released Parties&rdquo;</strong> means STEM+C and its current and former directors,
    officers, employees, coaches, mentors, volunteers, agents, insurers, affiliates, successors, and
    assigns, in each case only to the extent acting in connection with an Activity. The term also
    includes Activity hosts, facility owners and occupants, sponsors, competition organizers, and
    transportation providers identified in or covered by the registration materials.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Description and acknowledgment of risks</h2>
  <p>
    The Signing Parties understand that participation may expose the Participant to known and
    unknown risks that cannot be eliminated completely, even when reasonable safety measures are
    used. Depending on the Activity and the equipment then in use, risks may include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      designing, constructing, programming, testing, transporting, maintaining, and operating robots
      and mechanisms, including heavy robots, mechanisms, and subassemblies capable of rapid or
      unexpected movement;
    </li>
    <li>
      hand tools, portable power tools, and industrial or machine-shop equipment, which may include
      mills, lathes, CNC machines and routers, drill presses, saws, grinders, sanders, shears,
      brakes, presses, welding and cutting equipment, soldering equipment, laser cutters, 3D
      printers, hoists, lifts, and material-handling equipment;
    </li>
    <li>
      points of operation, rotating parts, belts, gears, blades, cutters, ingoing nip points,
      pinch/crush points, entanglement, kickback, ejected workpieces, flying chips and sparks, sharp
      edges and swarf, hot surfaces, molten material, and unexpected startup or release of stored
      mechanical, pneumatic, hydraulic, gravitational, thermal, or electrical energy;
    </li>
    <li>
      electricity, energized circuits, motors, control systems, chargers, batteries, battery acid,
      high current, fire, explosion, thermal runaway, compressed air, and compressed-gas cylinders;
    </li>
    <li>
      welding arc radiation, heat, flame, smoke, metal fumes, dust, vapors, adhesives, solvents,
      paints, lubricants, cleaning products, resins, and other chemicals or particulates;
    </li>
    <li>
      noise, vibration, inadequate ventilation, slips, trips, falls, lifting or moving heavy or
      awkward objects, falling objects, struck-by hazards, and repetitive motion or overexertion;
    </li>
    <li>
      the acts or omissions of the Participant, other participants, spectators, facility owners,
      event organizers, drivers, or other third parties; crowded public venues; weather; illness;
      food; and unfamiliar premises; and
    </li>
    <li>
      transportation in organization-arranged, volunteer-driven, rented, or privately owned
      vehicles; loading and unloading; overnight stays; and multi-day travel to regional or
      championship events.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These hazards may cause equipment or property damage; cuts, punctures, burns, eye or hearing
    injury, respiratory injury, electric shock, chemical exposure, allergic reaction, strains,
    fractures, crush injury, amputation, paralysis, illness, permanent disability, or death.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Safety obligations</h2>
  <p>
    The Participant agrees to follow all safety rules and instructions; complete required training;
    use required personal protective equipment; keep guards, barriers, interlocks, and other safety
    devices in place; avoid operating equipment without express authorization and required
    supervision; immediately report unsafe conditions, damaged equipment, injuries, and near misses;
    and stop work whenever the Participant believes a condition is unsafe. The Participant must not
    use equipment while impaired by alcohol, drugs, fatigue, illness, or medication that makes the
    work unsafe.
  </p>
  <p>
    STEM+C may restrict or end a Participant&rsquo;s access to any Activity or equipment for safety
    reasons. The Participant may decline or stop any task and should ask a coach or mentor for an
    alternative task when the Participant lacks training, authorization, appropriate protective
    equipment, or confidence that the task can be performed safely.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Voluntary participation and assumption of inherent risks</h2>
  <p>
    Participation is voluntary. The Signing Parties acknowledge the nature of the Activities and the
    risks described above, have had an opportunity to ask questions, and knowingly accept and assume
    the inherent and other risks of participation to the fullest extent permitted by Arizona law.
    The Signing Parties understand that this assumption of risk may be considered by a court or jury
    and is not a guarantee that every claim will be barred.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Release of claims and covenant not to sue</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, each adult Signing Party, for that adult
      and that adult&rsquo;s heirs, estate, personal representatives, and assigns, releases and agrees
      not to sue the Released Parties for claims for bodily injury, death, or property damage arising
      from or related to participation in the Activities, including claims alleging the ordinary
      negligence of a Released Party.
    </strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    This release does not apply to gross negligence, reckless or willful misconduct, intentional
    misconduct, or any other liability that cannot lawfully be released. It also does not waive any
    nonwaivable workers&rsquo; compensation or employment rights, or any rights or benefits available
    under an applicable insurance policy, although the insurer may have rights of reimbursement or
    subrogation.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the Participant is a minor, the Parent/Guardian signs this section in the Parent/Guardian&rsquo;s
    individual capacity and, only to the extent Arizona law permits, on behalf of the minor
    Participant. The parties acknowledge that a parent or guardian may not have authority to waive
    all claims belonging to a minor. Any separate parental indemnity must appear expressly in this
    Agreement; none is implied.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Responsibility for damage and third-party claims</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, an adult Participant is responsible for property damage or
    third-party injury caused by that adult Participant&rsquo;s intentional misconduct or negligent
    failure to follow safety rules. For a minor Participant, any Parent/Guardian responsibility or
    indemnity is limited to obligations that applicable law permits and that are stated expressly in
    this Agreement. This section does not require a Signing Party to indemnify a Released Party for
    that Released Party&rsquo;s own negligence.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Emergency information and medical authorization</h2>
  <p>
    The Participant or Parent/Guardian will provide accurate emergency-contact information and will
    disclose allergies, medical conditions, activity restrictions, and medications that STEM+C
    personnel reasonably need to know to respond to an emergency. The Signing Parties will keep that
    information current and may discuss necessary accommodations privately with a designated STEM+C
    representative.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the Participant becomes injured or ill and the appropriate Signing Party cannot be reached
    promptly, the Signing Parties authorize STEM+C personnel to provide or arrange reasonable first
    aid, emergency medical services, ambulance transportation, and evaluation or treatment by
    licensed medical professionals. This authorization does not require STEM+C personnel to diagnose
    a condition, provide professional medical care, or administer prescription medication except
    under a separate written medication plan. The Signing Parties remain responsible for medical
    costs not paid by insurance.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Optional media authorization</h2>
  <p>
    The media choice must be presented separately during registration and is not a condition of
    participation. The Participant or Parent/Guardian must select one of the following:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>I authorize program media.</strong> STEM+C may photograph, record, edit, reproduce,
      publish, display, and distribute the Participant&rsquo;s name, image, voice, statements, and
      submitted creative contributions in any medium for STEM+C educational, documentary,
      fundraising, and promotional purposes, without compensation. This permission includes use by
      vendors acting for STEM+C, but does not authorize endorsement of an unrelated commercial
      product or service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>I do not authorize program media.</strong> STEM+C will use reasonable efforts not to
      feature the Participant in media created or controlled by STEM+C. The Signing Parties
      understand that STEM+C cannot control incidental appearance in crowd or background images, or
      recordings made or published by FIRST, event hosts, sponsors, other teams, news media,
      spectators, or other third parties at public events.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A media choice may be changed prospectively by writing to
    <a href="mailto:info@stemplusc.org">info@stemplusc.org</a>. A change will not require recall or
    removal of material already printed, published, distributed, or incorporated into a completed
    work, but STEM+C will use reasonable efforts to stop new controlled uses after processing the
    request.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Term and other agreements</h2>
  <p>
    This Agreement applies to Activities during the 2026&ndash;2027 season, including authorized
    preseason and postseason Activities, and the provisions intended to survive participation remain
    effective afterward. This Agreement is separate from any consent, release, or registration that
    FIRST or an event host requires and from the
    <a href="/policies/team-agreement">STEM+C Student &amp; Family Team Agreement</a>. If another
    agreement conflicts with this Agreement, protections do not accumulate automatically.
  </p>

  <h2>9. General provisions</h2>
  <p>
    Arizona law governs this Agreement, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. If a provision is
    held invalid or unenforceable, it will be enforced to the maximum extent permitted and the
    remaining provisions will remain effective. No failure to enforce a safety rule or provision is
    a waiver of future enforcement. This Agreement contains the complete agreement on its subject
    matter and may be modified only in a written record accepted by STEM+C and the affected Signing
    Party. The headings are for convenience only.
  </p>

  <h2>Electronic acknowledgment and signatures</h2>
  <p>
    The registration system should display or provide a downloadable copy of this Agreement before
    acceptance and retain the accepted version, signer name and capacity, Participant name, date and
    time, and reliable audit information linking the signer to the record. The signing workflow
    includes separate acknowledgments for:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>the adult Participant, if the Participant is 18 or older;</li>
    <li>the Parent/Guardian, if the Participant is under 18;</li>
    <li>the minor Participant&rsquo;s acknowledgment of safety rules and instructions; and</li>
    <li>the optional media choice.</li>
  </ol>
</PolicyLayout>
